OWEN
I kept the lamp lit for thirty years. Every night I climbed those stairs. Every night I wound the clockwork. You were asleep, mostly. Your mother wasn't. She'd sit right there and read to me while the lens turned. I miss that more than anything. More than the sea, even. Promise me you'll keep it turning.

MARA
I promise.
